21
00:01:17,208 --> 00:01:20,971
The call The old machine is still here
because it works, roughly, and getting rid

22
00:01:20,971 --> 00:01:24,734
of something that works feels wasteful.

23
00:01:24,734 --> 00:01:28,498
Meanwhile it holds the corner and the new
one lives in the walking line.

24
00:01:28,498 --> 00:01:32,261
A spare is only a spare if it has actually
covered for the main one.

25
00:01:32,261 --> 00:01:36,024
So ask the question that decides it: in
the last year, did the main vacuum ever

26
00:01:36,024 --> 00:01:39,787
break down for long enough that you went
and got this one out?

27
00:01:39,787 --> 00:01:43,550
If the answer is no, it is not a backup,
it is a machine you are storing on behalf

28
00:01:43,550 --> 00:01:47,314
of a future that has not asked for it.

29
00:01:47,314 --> 00:01:51,077
Pass it to someone who has no vacuum at
all, and give the corner to the one you use

30
00:01:51,077 --> 00:01:54,840
every week.

